From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2026 04:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375: add fastrpc to the ADSP and CDSP

SM6375 has no fastrpc nodes, so the driver never probes and there is no
/dev/fastrpc, even though CONFIG_QCOM_FASTRPC builds fine and the module
is installed. Both remoteprocs already have a glink-edge; they just have
nothing under it but apr on the ADSP side.

The context bank stream IDs are the vendor's, out of holi.dtsi rather than
guessed from another SoC: 0x00a3..0x00a7 for the ADSP and 0x1001..0x1006
plus 0x1009 for the CDSP. They follow the same base-plus-bank-number
pattern sm6115 uses, which is a useful cross-check - getting a stream ID
wrong on this SoC is not a soft failure, a wrong SID copied from qcm2290
for camss bootlooped the device with no log output at all.

The ADSP node also needs a remote heap. Without a memory-region the probe
prints "no reserved DMA memory for FASTRPC" and any attempt to create a
static protection domain fails, which is exactly what a sensors PD needs.
The vmids come out agreeing from two directions: the vendor writes
qcom,adsp-remoteheap-vmid = <22 37>, and QCOM_SCM_VMID_LPASS is 0x16 with
QCOM_SCM_VMID_ADSP_HEAP 0x25, the same pair kodiak.dtsi uses. Size is 8 MB
in both trees. The region is declared the way the vendor does it, as a
reusable CMA pool with no fixed address, so it cannot collide with the
firmware carve-outs.

This is wanted for sensors. The accelerometer and gyroscope are on I3C
bus 1 and the magnetometers on the sensor core's own I2C bus 2, none of
which the application processor owns, so the only route to them is the
Snapdragon Sensor Core. That core is up and its framework sensors work,
but every physical sensor is missing because the registry sensor is
missing, and the registry lives on the AP.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
@@ -639,6 +639,14 @@
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			alloc-ranges = <0 0x00000000 0 0xffffffff>;
+			reusable;
+			alignment = <0 0x400000>;
+			size = <0 0x800000>;
+		};
+
 		cmdline_region: cmdline@ffd00000 {
 			reg = <0 0xffd00000 0 0x1000>;
 			no-map;
@@ -2144,6 +2152,48 @@
 						};
 					};
 				};
+
+				fastrpc {
+					compatible = "qcom,fastrpc";
+					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
+					label = "adsp";
+					qcom,non-secure-domain;
+					memory-region = <&adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem>;
+					qcom,vmids = <QCOM_SCM_VMID_LPASS
+						      QCOM_SCM_VMID_ADSP_HEAP>;
+					#address-cells = <1>;
+					#size-cells = <0>;
+
+					compute-cb@3 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <3>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x00a3 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@4 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <4>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x00a4 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@5 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <5>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x00a5 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@6 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <6>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x00a6 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@7 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <7>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x00a7 0x0>;
+					};
+				};
 			};
 		};
 
@@ -2180,6 +2230,57 @@
 						IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_GLINK_QMP>;
 				label = "cdsp";
 				qcom,remote-pid = <5>;
+
+				fastrpc {
+					compatible = "qcom,fastrpc";
+					qcom,glink-channels = "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp";
+					label = "cdsp";
+					qcom,non-secure-domain;
+					#address-cells = <1>;
+					#size-cells = <0>;
+
+					compute-cb@1 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <1>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1001 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@2 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <2>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1002 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@3 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <3>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1003 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@4 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <4>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1004 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@5 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <5>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1005 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@6 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <6>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1006 0x0>;
+					};
+
+					compute-cb@9 {
+						compatible = "qcom,fastrpc-compute-cb";
+						reg = <9>;
+						iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1009 0x0>;
+					};
+				};
 			};
 		};
 
